00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:24,000
No arrangement is more beautiful … or more complicated.

2
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:42,000
A Late Quartet is a music, drama film directed by Yaron Zilberman.

3
00:15:54,000 --> 00:16:00,000
When the beloved cellist of a world-renowned string quartet is diagnosed with a life threatening illness, the group's future suddenly hangs in the
balance as suppressed emotions, competing egos and uncontrollable passions threaten to derail years of friendship and collaboration.

4
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:18,000
As they are about to play their 25th anniversary concert — quite possibly their last —
only their intimate bond and the power of music can preserve their legacy.

5
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:36,000
Peter Mitchell, played by Christopher Walken.

6
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:54,000
Robert Gelbart, played by Philip Seymour Hoffman.

7
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:12,000
Daniel Lerner, played by Mark Ivanir.

8
00:42:24,000 --> 00:42:30,000
Juliette Gelbart, played by Catherine Keener.

9
00:47:42,000 --> 00:47:48,000
Alexandra Gelbart, played by Imogen Poots.

10
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:06,000
Pilar, played by Liraz Charhi.

11
00:58:18,000 --> 00:58:24,000
A Late Quartet (released in Australia as Performance) is a 2012 American drama film
directed by Yaron Zilberman and co-written by Zilberman and Seth Grossman.

12
01:03:36,000 --> 01:03:42,000
The film stars Philip Seymour Hoffman, Christopher Walken,
Catherine Keener, Mark Ivanir and Imogen Poots.

13
01:08:54,000 --> 01:09:00,000
Inspired by and structured around Beethoven's Op.

14
01:14:12,000 --> 01:14:18,000
131, the film follows the world-renowned Fugue String Quartet after its cellist
Peter Mitchell (Walken) is diagnosed with Parkinson's disease.

15
01:19:30,000 --> 01:19:36,000
Frederick Elmes served as cinematographer and
Angelo Badalamenti composed the score.

16
01:24:48,000 --> 01:24:54,000
The Brentano String Quartet played the quartet music for the soundtrack and Anne Sofie von Otter appears
as the cellist's late wife, singing Korngold's "Marietta's Song" from Die tote Stadt.

17
01:30:06,000 --> 01:30:12,000
The film premiered in the Special Presentation program at the 2012 Toronto
International Film Festival, and was theatrically released in over 30 countries.

18
01:35:24,000 --> 01:35:30,000
It received generally positive reviews.

19
01:40:42,000 --> 01:40:48,000
The tone is emotional.
